A header value containing a newline ( or 
) fails the value regex, so _validate_header_part raises InvalidHeader. The value validators are _VALID_HEADER_VALUE_RE_STR = re.compile(r"^\S[^
]*\Z|^\Z") and the bytes equivalent, which disallow  and 
 anywhere in the value (src/requests/_internal_utils.py:1-51). check_header_validity calls _validate_header_part for the name (index 0) and value (index 1) (src/requests/utils.py:1040-1095). _validate_header_part raises InvalidHeader with the message "Invalid leading whitespace, reserved character(s), or return character(s) in header value: ..." when the validator does not match (src/requests/utils.py:1098-1155). This is invoked from PreparedRequest.prepare_headers via check_header_validity (src/requests/models.py:565-574). InvalidHeader is defined as a RequestException/ValueError (src/requests/exceptions.py:102-162).
